   <title><![CDATA[Trump's Forgotten Take on Pride Month (Flashback Friday) [CrossPolitic Show]]]></title>
   <link/>
   <description><![CDATA[]]></description>
   <author><![CDATA[FLF, LLC]]></author>
   <enclosure url="https://app.dropwave.io/episode/e2f50d8a-207b-4032-82ba-769785f6a161/trumps-forgotten-take-on-pride-month-flashback-friday.mp3" length="2716" type="audio/mp3"/>
   <guid isPermaLink="false"><![CDATA[e2f50d8a-207b-4032-82ba-769785f6a161]]></guid>
   <pubDate>Sat, 21 Jun 2025 03:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
   <source url=""><![CDATA[FLF, LLC]]></source>
   <itunes:author><![CDATA[FLF, LLC]]></itunes:author>
   <itunes:summary><![CDATA[Trump once celebrated Pride Month—and most Christians forgot.

In this episode, we revisit a moment from Trump’s first presidency that many conservatives would rather ignore: his open endorsement of LGBT Pride Month. While evangelicals lined up behind him, the seeds of compromise were already planted. What does that moment reveal about the myth of neutrality? And what does it mean for Christians now, as the culture war escalates?

Toby, Gabe, Darren Doane, Doug Wilson, and Michael Dougherty break down why the public square was never neutral, why Trump’s past matters more than we think, and what kind of courage it will take for Christians to stop outsourcing conviction to politicians.]]></itunes:summary>
